id: pm-presets-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 quick PR and deep validation tiers
description: "Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required checks while moving exhaustive validation to deep CI, use deterministic quick seeded prefixes, retain unchanged coverage thresholds and Windows platform contracts."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: ci,performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T12:07:59.050Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T12:12:05.177Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-sol
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T12:08:01.577Z",codex-sol,"Oriented with context, CI/flaky searches and open items; no matching active CI tier task exists. Pilot pm-csv PR #258 reviewed. Required checks: test (22), test (26), windows-prepare-lifecycle. CodeQL is optional. Retain Windows parser/lifecycle contracts in quick CI and move duplicate simulation release gates into the full npm/Bun deep matrix. Release workflows and verifier scripts remain outside scope."
  "2026-11-15T12:11:29.073Z",codex-sol,"Latest successful main CI run 43679647905: created-to-completed test (22) 32m37s, test (26) 27m50s, simulation gates 27m37s, Windows 2m32s. Logs retrieved through the run archive because gh run view --log returned empty. Slowest full-depth packed test 154.33s, stack model 28.93s, parameter model 15.29s. Wave-1 PR #221 has one successful CI run and no failures. Quick prefixes cover seven property corpora without threshold changes; operational packed/lock/admission watchdogs scale by PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE. Packed acceptance runs artifacts under Bun but does not prove Bun package-manager/bunx installation; explicit graph-install and pinned bunx CLI smoke added."
  "2026-11-15T12:12:05.176Z",codex-sol,"Implemented quick/deep workflows and tier inventory. Typecheck, lint, build, test compilation and four CI/depth/watchdog contract tests passed (linked command 3.66s). Strict YAML parsing passed for all three workflows, with explicit timeouts on every job; actionlint is unavailable. Targeted quick tests are running. Push early for authoritative hosted CI feedback; local quick coverage will be bounded to 20 minutes. No full-depth suite is run locally."
